{
  "title": "Big-endian integers",
  "function": "read_u32_be",
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "data",
      "type": "bytes"
    },
    {
      "name": "offset",
      "type": "int"
    }
  ],
  "returns": "int",
  "library": true,
  "hints": [
    "Each byte is a base-256 digit, and the first byte is the most significant.",
    "value = data[o]·256³ + data[o+1]·256² + data[o+2]·256 + data[o+3]; with shifts: (b0 << 24) | (b1 << 16) | (b2 << 8) | b3.",
    "In Rust and C++, convert each byte to a wider type (usize / std::size_t) before shifting, or the bits fall off the top of a u8."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          8,
          3
        ],
        0
      ],
      "description": "the IDX magic number for an image file",
      "expected": 2051
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          39,
          16
        ],
        0
      ],
      "description": "10,000: the number of MNIST test images",
      "expected": 10000
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          9,
          9,
          0,
          0,
          234,
          96
        ],
        2
      ],
      "description": "60,000, starting at offset 2",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 60000
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ],
        0
      ],
      "description": "every byte matters",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 16909060
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          255,
          255,
          255,
          255
        ],
        0
      ],
      "description": "the largest 32-bit value",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 4294967295
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          1
        ],
        0
      ],
      "description": "only 3 bytes left",
      "expect_error": true,
      "hidden": true
    }
  ]
}
